    "result_text": "I added `_allow_redirect` to `hc/accounts/views.py`, above `_make_user`. I haven't run the tests or the app, but the pcat `check_code` found no deviations from the reviewed pattern.\n\nThe file already called `_allow_redirect` in four places but never defined it. Those calls are in the login view's magic-link branch, `_redirect_after_login`, `_check_2fa` and `login_webauthn`. Any of them would have raised `NameError` at runtime. The login view uses the helper through those calls, so I didn't change any of them.\n\nThe helper comes from the catalog pattern `accounts.allow_redirect@v1`, and I kept its `# pcat:` marker above it. It allows a `next` URL only if:\n- it is non-empty,\n- it has no host (so no redirects to other sites), and\n- its path resolves to one of the routes in `POST_LOGIN_ROUTES` (`hc-checks`, `hc-details`, `hc-log` and so on).\n\n`POST_LOGIN_ROUTES` and the imports it needs (`urlparse`, `resolve`, `Resolver404`) were already in the file."
